    "history_summary": [
      {
        "value": "Easter Eggers are American hybrids created by breeding a bird carrying the blue-egg gene, descended from Chilean Araucana stock, with brown-egg-laying breeds. They are not recognized as a breed by the American Poultry Association or American Bantam Association, but became popular backyard and hatchery birds for their variable, colorful eggs.",
